*> Experience orb value tiers (docs/protocol/21 section 8.2 and the worked example E6 of section 9; lane 002-lane-p49e, T18520): value(total) at and just below each of the ten
*> tiers, and the split of 960 into orbs of 617, 307, 17, 17, 1 and 1.
 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. TEST-MOB-21-8-2.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 COPY TESTLIB.
 01 WS-TIERS-DATA.
    05 FILLER BINARY-LONG VALUE 2477.
    05 FILLER BINARY-LONG VALUE 1237.
    05 FILLER BINARY-LONG VALUE 617.
    05 FILLER BINARY-LONG VALUE 307.
    05 FILLER BINARY-LONG VALUE 149.
    05 FILLER BINARY-LONG VALUE 73.
    05 FILLER BINARY-LONG VALUE 37.
    05 FILLER BINARY-LONG VALUE 17.
    05 FILLER BINARY-LONG VALUE 7.
    05 FILLER BINARY-LONG VALUE 3.
    05 FILLER BINARY-LONG VALUE 1.
 01 WS-TIERS REDEFINES WS-TIERS-DATA.
    05 WS-TIER             BINARY-LONG OCCURS 11 TIMES.
 01 WS-I                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-TOTAL               BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-VALUE               BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-N                   PIC 9(4).
 01 WS-E                   PIC ZZZ9.
 01 WS-SEQ                 PIC X(40).
 01 WS-P                   BINARY-LONG.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION.
     MOVE "N" TO TL-MODE
     PERFORM VARYING WS-I FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-I > 10
         MOVE WS-TIER(WS-I) TO WS-TOTAL
         CALL "XP-ORB-VALUE" USING WS-TOTAL WS-VALUE
         MOVE WS-TIER(WS-I) TO WS-N
         STRING "acceptance US15 21§8.2 Experience orb: the value of " DELIMITED BY SIZE WS-N DELIMITED BY SIZE
             " is itself" DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-CASE
         MOVE WS-TIER(WS-I) TO TL-EXPECTED-N
         MOVE WS-VALUE TO TL-OBSERVED-N
         CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
         COMPUTE WS-TOTAL = WS-TIER(WS-I) - 1
         CALL "XP-ORB-VALUE" USING WS-TOTAL WS-VALUE
         STRING "acceptance US15 21§8.2 Experience orb: the value of " DELIMITED BY SIZE WS-N DELIMITED BY SIZE
             " less one is the next tier down" DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-CASE
         MOVE WS-TIER(WS-I + 1) TO TL-EXPECTED-N
         MOVE WS-VALUE TO TL-OBSERVED-N
         CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     END-PERFORM
     MOVE 5000 TO WS-TOTAL
     CALL "XP-ORB-VALUE" USING WS-TOTAL WS-VALUE
     MOVE "acceptance US15 21§8.2 Experience orb: no tier is above 2477" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 2477 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-VALUE TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
*>   E6: repeat v = value(total), total = total - v.
     MOVE 960 TO WS-TOTAL
     MOVE 0 TO WS-P
     MOVE 0 TO WS-I
     PERFORM UNTIL WS-TOTAL <= 0
         CALL "XP-ORB-VALUE" USING WS-TOTAL WS-VALUE
         SUBTRACT WS-VALUE FROM WS-TOTAL
         ADD 1 TO WS-I
         MOVE WS-VALUE TO WS-E
         MOVE FUNCTION CONCATENATE(FUNCTION TRIM(WS-SEQ), " ", FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E)) TO WS-SEQ
     END-PERFORM
     MOVE "acceptance US15 21§9 Worked examples E6: 960 makes six orbs" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 6 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-I TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE "acceptance US15 21§9 Worked examples E6: the orbs are 617 307 17 17 1 1" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "A" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE "617 307 17 17 1 1" TO TL-EXPECTED
     MOVE FUNCTION TRIM(WS-SEQ) TO TL-OBSERVED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     STOP RUN.
 END PROGRAM TEST-MOB-21-8-2.
